# Contributing to {{ projectName }}

Keep changes focused and review public HTTP paths, operation IDs, environment names, and database migration effects before committing. `PROJECT.md` and `SERVICE.md` belong to this application. Use a short branch and a clear `type(scope): intent` title; report actual checks and the compatibility decision in the PR.

## Local checks

Commit `uv.lock` after the first render, then use the same commands as CI:

```bash
uv lock --check
uv sync --locked
uv run --locked ruff check .
uv run --locked ruff format --check .
uv run --locked mypy
{% if withTesting %}uv run --locked pytest -q
{% endif %}uv build
```

The generated tests cover infrastructure HTTP and lifecycle behavior when `withTesting=true`. Add tests for real product behavior as it appears. Positive database readiness and Alembic upgrades require an isolated PostgreSQL instance. A wheel build, image build, release, and deployment are distinct operations.
